Next      PREDICTION PARTLY WRONG, and the miss is informative: UGBW went UP
          (9.43 -> 17.61), not down. Reason: the nfets sit at gm/id ~ 23-26, i.e.
          moderate-to-weak inversion, where gm tracks CURRENT and is nearly
          independent of W/L -- so lengthening cost almost no gm, while fixing
          the mirror's Vds error RAISED the tail current 26.34 -> 43.40 uA.
          gm1 rose 62%. Two problems left, both small: PM 47.09 is below the 50
          floor, and Power 0.6049 is 4% over the real ceiling.
          R0 = 100 ohm against 1/gm2 = 460 ohm -- the nulling resistor is 4.6x
          UNDER-sized, so the RHP zero is not being cancelled at all. Sizing R0
          ABOVE 1/gm2 turns it into an LHP zero that can cancel the output pole:
          a large PM gain for zero current. That is iteration 2.

