Reasoning XMP4 is the self_biased_reference's smaller device and therefore sets
          I_ref for every mirror leg (circuit_decomposition.yaml xpd2). Cutting
          its width was predicted to cut I_ref and, through net7, every leg
          current with it -- buying a large Power reduction.
Next      LANDED HARD -- and OVERSHOT in the other direction. Power fell 34%
          below its ceiling (0.383 vs 0.5813), but the leg currents fell with it
          and gm1 dropped 33%, taking UGBW from 18.20 down to 11.95 -- now the
          ONLY failing key, short by 3.05 MHz.
          This is a good position, not a bad one: the design now has 22.4 dB of
          Gain margin and 0.199 mW (110 uA) of unspent Power headroom against
          ONE key that misses by 20%. The correction is to put a fraction of
          that current back into the SIGNAL path rather than the bias leg --
          i.e. raise the tail ratio MN3_M, which is exactly the mirror-ratio
          lever this contract made tunable. UGBW ~ gm1/(2*pi*Cc) and gm1 tracks
          current at gm/id ~ 26, so MN3_M 2 -> 3 should give ~1.5x gm1.
          PM will fall as UGBW rises (p2 = gm2/CL is unchanged); PM 65.78 has
          ~15.8 deg of room down to the 50 floor, so there is margin to spend.

