Op-point  IDENTICAL to iteration 3 in every device, to 4 decimal places.
Reasoning UGBW ~ gm1/(2*pi*Cc) and gm1 is set by the tail CURRENT (gm/id ~ 26,
          i.e. moderate/weak inversion, where gm tracks id and barely responds
          to width). Two ways to raise UGBW: more current, or less Cc. The
          objective is every key met at MINIMUM POWER, so the current-free lever
          goes first. Predicted UGBW x1.40 and a PM fall.
Next      UGBW rose x1.287, not the x1.402 that 1/Cc alone predicts -- so net5
          and vout carry fixed capacitance beyond Cc, and Cc's authority over
          UGBW is sub-linear (exponent ~0.75). The op-point being bit-identical
          CONFIRMS Cc is a pure AC lever with no DC cost. First state in the run
          with all four REAL keys met, and at 0.383 mW. Harder UGBW short 1.12
          MHz. Budget remains, so keep aiming at the harder bar -- UGBW is
          precisely the key layout parasitics eat.

