Reasoning Cc alone would have landed PM near 53.5 (extrapolating iteration 3->4's
          -37.3 deg per natural-log of UGBW). xpd1 in the circuit read says R0
          and Cc are one network: the LHP zero sits at 1/(Cc*(R0 - 1/gm2)), so
          shrinking Cc moves the zero and R0 must be re-sized to keep it doing
          its job. Raised R0 with Cc to hold the zero near the output pole.
Next      LANDED BETTER THAN PREDICTED: PM 56.96, about 3.5 deg above the
          Cc-only extrapolation -- that difference is the retuned zero, and it
          is the reason this converged instead of scraping the harder PM floor.
          Stopping here per stop condition 1. Iteration 7 of 8 left UNSPENT:
          the budget is a ceiling, not a quota, and gilding a met spec risks it.

